## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical app registration for a mobile app using PKCE with Azure AD, focusing on public client setup, permissions, and cleanup.

## Key Concepts

- Public client app registration
- Redirect URIs for mobile apps
- API permissions and consent
- PKCE flow basics
- Token validation and cleanup

## Code Example

```javascript
// MSAL config for a mobile app
const msalConfig = {
  auth: {
    clientId: "YOUR_CLIENT_ID",
    authority: "https://login.microsoftonline.com/YOUR_TENANT_ID",
    redirectUri: "com.example.app://auth"
  },
  cache: { cacheLocation: "localStorage" }
};
const loginRequest = { scopes: ["User.Read"] };
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend this for multi-tenant access?
- What changes if the app transitions to a confidential client?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical use of PIM, approvals, MFA, and auditing in real admin flows.

## Key Concepts

- Privileged Identity Management
- Just-In-Time access
- MFA and approvals
- Activation duration and auto-revoke
- Auditing and alerts

## Code Example

```javascript
// PIM-like REST flow (illustrative)
async function activatePIM() {
  const token = await getGraphToken(['PrivilegedIdentityManagement.Read.All']);
  const res = await fetch('https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/privilegedRoleAssignments', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${token}`, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      roleDefinitionId: '<role-id>',
      scope: '<scope>',
      duration: 'PT1H',
      activationApprover: '<manager@contoso.com>'
    })
  });
  return res.json();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle emergency access without cascading approvals?
- What CA or BA policies would guard this flow during off-hours?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of Azure AD B2B, group licensing, Conditional Access, and governance with Access Reviews. It also checks how candidates validate access during and after a time window.

## Key Concepts
- Azure AD B2B guest onboarding
- Group-based licensing
- Conditional Access MFA for guests
- Access Reviews and auto‑revocation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Graph API (pseudocode) invites a guest and adds to a guest group
async function inviteGuest(email) {
  await graphClient.api('/invitations').post({ invitedUserEmailAddress: email, inviteRedirectUrl: 'https://portal' });
  // add to guests group
  await graphClient.api(`/groups/{guestGroupId}/members/$ref`).post({ "@odata.id": `https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/users/${guestId}` });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle license revocation if a guest leaves early?
- How would you monitor for guests with elevated access beyond 14 days?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical mastery of Azure AD risk-based access controls at scale, including how to design policies, test them safely, and rollback without service disruption.

## Key Concepts

- Identity Protection risk scoring
- Conditional Access policies
- MFA and device compliance
- Session controls and continuous access evaluation
- SIEM integration and audit trails
- Safe rollback and access-review processes

## Code Example

```json
{
  "conditionalAccessPolicy": {
    "displayName": "Risk-based admin access",
    "conditions": {
      "users": { "include": ["admin@contoso.com"] },
      "signInRiskLevels": ["high","medium"],
      "platforms": { "include": ["All"] }
    },
    "grantControls": {
      "builtInControls": ["mfa","deviceCompliance"],
      "sessionControls": ["requireUserConsent","limitSessionDuration"]
    },
    "applications": ["https://portal.contoso.com/admin"]
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate these policies in a sandbox before production?
- How would you measure impact on admin productivity and detect policy drift?
